 b1216d0cda3, rebased on 9ddb035cf59) failed `tests/unit/test_snapshot_janitor.py::test_byte_total_consistent_under_concurrent_populate_evict` at `tests/unit/test_snapshot_janitor.py:188`: `assert 312 == 365` (`cache.byte_total(store)` against `_real_store_bytes(store)`). The host was running a second `make verify` at the same time. The test passed 3 of 3 times rerun alone. The branch does not touch `src/rebar/_snapshot/` (its only POSIX-visible change routes `fsutil.atomic_write` through a helper that is exactly `os.replace` off Windows).\n\n## Hypotheses (unproven)\n- The running byte counter (`cache.add_bytes`, under `interprocess_lock`) and the populate/evict paths disagree on what a racing populate or evict adds or frees (for example a populate that loses the single-flight race, or `_evict`'s `exclusive_size` measured before a concurrent hardlink change).\n- The assertion reads the walk while a populate is still finishing.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The interleaving that produces the drift is reproduced deterministically and recorded on this ticket.\n- [ ] The byte total matches the store walk under that interleaving, with a regression test.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["flaky","snapshot"],"ticket_id":"3822-a9e3-5999-422c","ticket_type":"bug","title":"test_byte_total_consistent_under_concurrent_populate_evict: byte total drifts from the store walk under host load","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["2b5f9515-77a6-467f-b255-c9185c10ecbe","13cf9122-9b55-4e7d-9dd2-c4d7a5ab6e62"]},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1795047654119134091,"uuid":"3462befd-c313-4f23-89a4-6ef5cc98895f"}
